Do not cache inference results that were truncated by the inference budget.

``NodeNG.infer`` appends an ``Uninferable`` placeholder once the per-inference
budget (``InferenceContext.max_inferred``) is exhausted, and used to store that
truncated tuple in the process-wide inference cache. Because that cache is
shared by every module, a later inference of the same node with a fresh budget
returned the cached ``Uninferable`` even though the node was inferable, which
made results depend on the order in which the modules were analysed.

Refs #3383
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#11582
